<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Donnus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Donnus was a king of the Alpine peoples around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/susa-piedmont">Segusio</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/susa">Susa</a>) and the Montgenèvre pass in the 1st century BCE, in the time of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>. He was the father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-julius-cottius">Marcus Julius Cottius</a>, who made peace with Augustus and governed the region as a Roman prefect; the inscription on his son's arch at Susa names Cottius as son of King Donnus.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/donnus.jpg" alt="Donnus" width="320" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hibernian · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Augustan_Arch,_Susa.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
